<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Captaincy General of Guatemala</h1><p class="st-meta">1524 CE – 1821 CE · capital Santiago de los Caballeros</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Spanish Kingdom of Guatemala, which governed Central America from Chiapas to Costa Rica for nearly three centuries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-alvarado">Pedro de Alvarado</a> conquered the highland Maya kingdoms from 1524 and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigua-guatemala">Santiago de los Caballeros</a>, first at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kaqchikel-kingdom">Iximche</a>. The capital moved to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ciudad-vieja">Almolonga</a> valley and, after a mudflow in 1541, to present-day <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-antigua">Antigua</a>. An audiencia was established in 1543 and seated in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-jamaica">Santiago</a> from 1549.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Captaincy General, nominally under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/new-spain">New Spain</a>, governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiapas">Chiapas</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-guatemala">Guatemala</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-el-salvador">El Salvador</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-honduras">Honduras</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-nicaragua">Nicaragua</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-costa-rica">Costa Rica</a>. Its economy rested on indigenous tribute and labour, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cacao">cacao</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indigo">indigo</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartolome-de-las-casas">Bartolomé de las Casas</a> led peaceful missions in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verapaz">Verapaz</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-jamaica">Santiago</a> was a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> architecture and learning until earthquakes in 1773 led to the founding of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala-city">Guatemala City</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a> declared independence on 15 September 1821, joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-mexican-empire">First Mexican Empire</a> briefly, and in 1823 formed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/federal-republic-of-central-america">Federal Republic of Central America</a>, except <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiapas">Chiapas</a>, which stayed with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mexico">Mexico</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/captaincy-general-of-guatemala.jpg" alt="Captaincy General of Guatemala" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Ningyou. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cross_of_Burgundy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1524 CE – 1821 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Santiago de los Caballeros</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pedro de Alvarado, Gabino Gaínza</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, <a href="/countries/el-salvador">El Salvador</a>, <a href="/countries/honduras">Honduras</a>, <a href="/countries/nicaragua">Nicaragua</a>, <a href="/countries/costa-rica">Costa Rica</a>, <a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Guatemala, Audiencia of Guatemala, Reino de Guatemala</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1672&amp;focus=captaincy-general-of-guatemala" aria-label="Captaincy General of Guatemala on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2198 1636 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Captaincy General of